 "meta": {
  "bibkey": "solstad-bott-2024",
  "method": "experiment",
  "description": "The three rating experiments on German occasion verbs. Block 1 of Experiments 1 and 2: the acceptability of a trigger's sentence in a neutral context, after a sentence supplying the projective content (anaphoric) and before one (cataphoric), on a slider transformed to [0, 1], with the likelihood-ratio tests of a supported context against the neutral one. Block 2: the projectivity and at-issueness of the occasion implication and of the implications of stimulus-experiencer and experiencer-stimulus psychological verbs, in the paradigm of Tonhauser, Beaver and Degen (2018), with 1 the maximal projectivity and the maximal at-issueness; the established triggers run alongside are plotted only. Experiment 3: the projectivity of the content from a conditional antecedent holding the trigger alone, before a conjunct entailing the content, or after one.",
